WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.192
Module three. Warehouses. Where the goods are picked up from, and why the admin must

2
00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:07.989
Verify every pickup address.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.081
Every S K U lives in a warehouse, and every order is picked up from a warehouse.

4
00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:19.779
If the warehouse is wrong, nothing else works. So let's get warehouses right.

5
00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:21.957
First, the warehouses page.

6
00:00:22.407 --> 00:00:24.860
Then adding a new warehouse, field by field.

7
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.702
Why a new warehouse stays pending until the admin approves it.

8
00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:33.355
The new agreed process for verifying the pickup address in Shiprocket.

9
00:00:33.805 --> 00:00:38.477
And the buttons on each warehouse card: pause intake, staff and view inventory.

10
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:43.000
This is the vendor's warehouses page.

11
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.248
Active warehouses. How many pickup locations the vendor has.

12
00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:50.343
Capacity. The total space, in square feet.

13
00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:54.612
Open orders. Orders still to be fulfilled from these warehouses.

14
00:00:55.062 --> 00:00:58.987
Total S K Us live. Products that customers can buy right now.

15
00:00:59.437 --> 00:01:00.888
The Add warehouse button.

16
00:01:01.338 --> 00:01:04.801
And each card shows a status. Approved means it can sell.

17
00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:07.354
Pending means it is waiting for the admin.

18
00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:13.372
Before we watch it, here is every field on the add warehouse form.

19
00:01:13.822 --> 00:01:18.157
Pickup location name. Use a clear name, like the city plus a number.

20
00:01:18.157 --> 00:01:19.305
It must be unique.

21
00:01:19.755 --> 00:01:24.510
Full address and pincode. This is the exact address the courier will come to.

22
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.795
Spelling and pincode must be correct.

23
00:01:27.245 --> 00:01:28.760
Capacity in square feet.

24
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.818
Opening and closing time. Pickups are only scheduled inside these hours.

25
00:01:34.268 --> 00:01:37.972
Pin the exact location on Google Map, or use Locate Me.

26
00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:40.262
Drag the pin to the real entrance.

27
00:01:40.712 --> 00:01:45.254
And the vehicle types that can reach the warehouse, from mini truck to trailer, plus

28
00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:46.174
Warehouse photos.

29
00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.487
Let's watch this in the live demo.

30
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.785
Here is the live demo. The vendor opens Warehouses.

31
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.087
And clicks Add warehouse.

32
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.820
The form opens. Name, pincode, capacity, timings, map and vehicle types.

33
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:17.718
The vendor names it Gorakhpur one, enters the address, and the pincode two seven

34
00:02:17.718 --> 00:02:18.972
Three zero zero one.

35
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.855
Opening time nine in the morning, closing time six in the evening.

36
00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.585
Then the pin on the map. The tip says: click anywhere on the map or drag the pin to

37
00:02:37.585 --> 00:02:39.292
The exact warehouse entrance.

38
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.656
Next, the allowed vehicles. Mini truck, light commercial vehicle, medium and heavy

39
00:02:46.656 --> 00:02:48.668
Commercial vehicle, and trailer.

40
00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.828
Photos are added, and the warehouse is saved.

41
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.947
The new card, Gorakhpur one, appears first, with the status pending.

42
00:02:56.947 --> 00:02:58.759
It cannot receive orders yet.

43
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.380
Each card has Pause Intake, Staff and View inventory.

44
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.113
We'll come to those shortly.

45
00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:28.444
On the admin side, the vendor's details page lists every store and warehouse.

46
00:03:28.894 --> 00:03:31.283
A pending warehouse, like Gorakhpur one.

47
00:03:31.733 --> 00:03:33.248
The admin can approve it.

48
00:03:33.698 --> 00:03:36.578
Or reject it, for example if the address is wrong.

49
00:03:37.028 --> 00:03:41.760
Once approved, the badge turns to approved, and products in this warehouse can be

50
00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.279
Shown to nearby customers.

51
00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:50.226
In the live session, the team found a real problem, and agreed on a fix.

52
00:03:50.226 --> 00:03:53.582
This is important, so let's compare before and after.

53
00:03:54.032 --> 00:03:58.595
Before. A warehouse got approved, a customer ordered, and the vendor tried to

54
00:03:58.595 --> 00:04:03.515
Dispatch through Shiprocket. But Shiprocket had never verified that pickup address,

55
00:04:03.515 --> 00:04:06.597
So the vendor saw an error, and the order got stuck.

56
00:04:07.047 --> 00:04:10.770
Now. When a vendor adds a warehouse, the admin is notified.

57
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:15.880
The admin first verifies the pickup address in Shiprocket, and only then approves

58
00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:21.054
The warehouse. So by the time any order comes in, the address is already verified,

59
00:04:21.054 --> 00:04:23.388
And the vendor never sees that error.

60
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.173
Here is exactly how the admin verifies a pickup address in Shiprocket.

61
00:04:30.623 --> 00:04:33.013
Log in to the Oribrix Shiprocket account.

62
00:04:33.463 --> 00:04:34.465
Open Settings.

63
00:04:34.915 --> 00:04:36.259
Go to Company Setup.

64
00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:40.976
Open Pick Up Addresses. The new warehouse appears here as unverified.

65
00:04:41.426 --> 00:04:46.668
Click verify. An O T P goes to the phone number registered for that pickup address.

66
00:04:46.668 --> 00:04:49.383
Enter it, and the address becomes verified.

67
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:53.375
Only then, go back to the admin panel and approve the warehouse.

68
00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:59.210
This was agreed in the session, so treat it as a rule.

69
00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:04.119
Never approve a warehouse whose pickup address is not verified in Shiprocket.

70
00:05:04.119 --> 00:05:09.410
Verify first, approve second. Vendors should never see a pickup verification error.

71
00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.215
If one does, it means this step was skipped.

72
00:05:47.933 --> 00:05:52.968
Back on the vendor side. View inventory on a card opens that warehouse's stock.

73
00:05:53.418 --> 00:05:55.466
How many S K Us are in this warehouse.

74
00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:57.366
The total stock value.

75
00:05:57.816 --> 00:05:59.331
How many are low on stock.

76
00:05:59.781 --> 00:06:02.789
And each S K U, with brand, stock and price.

77
00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.312
Every warehouse card has a few buttons.

78
00:06:07.762 --> 00:06:12.459
Pause Intake. Temporarily hides this warehouse's items from customers.

79
00:06:12.459 --> 00:06:16.082
Useful during a holiday, a stock count, or a shortage.

80
00:06:16.532 --> 00:06:19.668
Staff. Shows which staff logins can work on this warehouse.

81
00:06:20.118 --> 00:06:23.787
View inventory. Shows the S K Us and stock in this warehouse.

82
00:06:24.237 --> 00:06:29.233
Edit, the pencil icon. Editing a warehouse sends it back to pending, for the admin

83
00:06:29.233 --> 00:06:30.147
To check again.

84
00:06:30.597 --> 00:06:33.455
And open or closed, which shows today's status.

85
00:06:35.867 --> 00:06:38.753
Most warehouse problems start with a careless form.

86
00:06:38.753 --> 00:06:42.374
Before a vendor clicks save, they should check these six things.

87
00:06:42.824 --> 00:06:47.508
The name is clear and unique, for example the city plus a number, so staff and

88
00:06:47.508 --> 00:06:49.309
Couriers know which one it is.

89
00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:52.783
The address matches the real gate, with a landmark.

90
00:06:52.783 --> 00:06:54.324
Couriers follow this text.

91
00:06:54.774 --> 00:06:59.404
The pincode is correct. A wrong pincode can make Shiprocket reject the pickup.

92
00:06:59.854 --> 00:07:04.120
The map pin is dragged to the actual entrance, not just the middle of the city.

93
00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:09.392
The opening and closing times match when staff are really there to hand over goods.

94
00:07:09.842 --> 00:07:15.031
And the phone number on the account is real and answered, because O T Ps and pickup

95
00:07:15.031 --> 00:07:16.156
Messages go there.

96
00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:23.112
The map pin decides which customers see the vendor's stock, and where the courier

97
00:07:23.112 --> 00:07:25.692
Goes. Let's compare a good pin with a bad one.

98
00:07:26.142 --> 00:07:30.393
A good pin sits on the warehouse gate, in the same area as the address.

99
00:07:30.393 --> 00:07:35.124
Nearby customers see the stock, and the courier finds the place the first time.

100
00:07:35.574 --> 00:07:39.174
A bad pin sits in the city centre, or even in another city.

101
00:07:39.174 --> 00:07:42.042
The address says one place and the pin another.

102
00:07:42.042 --> 00:07:46.131
The wrong customers see the stock, and pickups fail or get delayed.

103
00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:50.891
When you review a warehouse as admin, always compare the pin with the address.

104
00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:57.669
When someone says a product isn't showing in the customer app, go through this list

105
00:07:57.669 --> 00:07:58.143
In order.

106
00:07:58.593 --> 00:08:01.857
Is the warehouse approved? Pending warehouses don't sell.

107
00:08:02.307 --> 00:08:05.528
Is intake paused? Then the items are hidden on purpose.

108
00:08:05.978 --> 00:08:09.711
Is the S K U in stock? Out of stock items can't be ordered.

109
00:08:10.161 --> 00:08:14.663
Is the customer near this warehouse? Customers only see nearby warehouses.

110
00:08:15.113 --> 00:08:19.742
And is the vendor account suspended? We'll cover suspension in module six.

111
00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:25.607
Quick check. A vendor added a new warehouse ten minutes ago.

112
00:08:25.607 --> 00:08:29.024
What must the admin do before approving it? Think about it.

113
00:08:32.974 --> 00:08:38.255
The answer: verify the pickup address in Shiprocket, under Settings, Company Setup,

114
00:08:38.255 --> 00:08:40.291
Pick Up Addresses. Then approve.

115
00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:47.043
Before we finish, here are the warehouse words once more, in the order a new

116
00:08:47.043 --> 00:08:48.496
Warehouse goes through them.

117
00:08:48.946 --> 00:08:52.616
Pickup location. The warehouse address the courier comes to.

118
00:08:53.066 --> 00:08:56.906
Pending. The warehouse is saved, and waiting for the admin's checks.

119
00:08:57.356 --> 00:09:02.390
Verified, in Shiprocket. The pickup address has been confirmed with an O T P.

120
00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:06.190
Approved. The warehouse can now sell to nearby customers.

121
00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:11.333
And paused. The vendor has hidden its items for now, and can resume any time.

122
00:09:13.733 --> 00:09:18.217
One more check. A vendor's warehouse will be closed for Diwali for three days.

123
00:09:18.217 --> 00:09:20.517
What should they do? Think for a moment.

124
00:09:24.467 --> 00:09:27.923
The answer: pause intake, and resume it after Diwali.

125
00:09:27.923 --> 00:09:33.075
Deleting the warehouse or zeroing stock creates extra work, and a new warehouse

126
00:09:33.075 --> 00:09:34.771
Would need approval again.

127
00:09:37.566 --> 00:09:39.315
Let's summarise module three.

128
00:09:39.765 --> 00:09:43.051
A warehouse is an exact pickup address, with a map pin.

129
00:09:43.501 --> 00:09:45.570
A new or edited warehouse is pending.

130
00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:49.519
The admin first verifies the pickup address in Shiprocket.

131
00:09:49.969 --> 00:09:51.889
Then the admin approves the warehouse.

132
00:09:52.339 --> 00:09:57.598
And pause intake hides the items temporarily. Next, in module four, orders and

133
00:09:57.598 --> 00:09:58.205
Dispatch.

134
00:10:00.599 --> 00:10:05.250
That's the end of module 3. Next up, module 4: Orders and dispatch.
